# werewolf's own security advisories: fixes to werewolf's code, which no
# CVE names (docs/design/update-policy.md, werewolf's own fixes). Add a
# line in the commit that makes the fix:
#
#   ID           DATE        TIER    TITLE
#   WW-2026-001  2026-10-07  high    fence: what was wrong, in a line
#
# ID is WW-YEAR-NUMBER, never reused; DATE when the fix landed, UTC; TIER
# urgent, high, medium or low, as a CVE of the same weight would be; TITLE
# printable ASCII, no quotes or backslashes, at most 200 characters. Every
# image carries this file, so it knows which fixes it has. CI publishes it
# as werewolf-advisories, and a machine applies each advisory its next slot
# lists and its own image lacks at its tier (cmd/slot-update). make test
# refuses a line it cannot read (lib/update-policy.zig).
